35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! It looks like almost all the complaints come from just one house. That's so sad! We really need to find a way to help them out so everyone can be happy again!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is very heartbreaking to hear, Kenji. It is no wonder there has been tension if one neighbor has been suffering alone. We must be very gentle and thoughtful in how we support them.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings confirm that the burden is not just social, but physical. The frontages are vastly unequal; some cannot even accommodate a bay. We cannot simply maintain the status quo or ignore these physical disparities in our planning.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found some secrets! The bin house at the station block smells super sour in the summer because you can't wash the floor! Yucky! But the next lane has a ""supervised morning"" club that's only 20 times a year!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is enlightening to hear your discoveries. I have found that we spend thirty-four thousand yen annually on maintenance due to open bags, and new shelters are quite costly, even with the ward's forty percent subsidy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, a ""supervised morning club"" sounds like a fun way to do it! But @Servas, if new shelters are so expensive, maybe we should find a way that doesn't cost too much money, so no one gets stressed about it!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, thank you for sharing. I also found that the bin house can become quite unpleasant in the summer heat. It would be a shame to trade one worry for another and make our streets less inviting.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, while a ""club"" sounds pleasant, we must consider the actual labor. My research into the station block shows that structures often lead to disputes over maintenance and cleaning. We need a system that doesn't create new burdens.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're so serious! But if we take turns, it's not a burden, it's like a team game! @Kenji, I agree! We should pick something that's fair and doesn't cost a mountain of money!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your youthful energy is a gift to us all. However, we must remember that a ""team game"" still requires a shared cost. We must be mindful that our neighbors' budgets vary as much as their frontages do.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, you're right! We have to be careful. But I also found that nobody wants to be the ""bad guy"" who tells neighbors their bags are late. If we pick a plan that's too strict, it might just make people fight more!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, that is a very thoughtful point. We must avoid any system that makes our neighbors feel judged or uncomfortable. A gentle approach, where we support one another, will be much more sustainable for our hearts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, that is precisely why we must avoid vague agreements. When rules are unclear, the responsibility inevitably falls on the person who is most compliant or the one who answers the phone first. We need a concrete system.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right about the rules! But we have to make sure the ""concrete system"" doesn't just leave the trash at the same house's gate forever. That wouldn't be a team game at all, it would be cheating!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you speak a great truth. Fairness is not merely about the rules, but about the spirit in which they are applied. Let us seek a path that balances the physical burden with a financial weight that no one finds impossible to carry.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I really hope we can find a way to stop the fighting! If we can just make sure the person who's been complaining feels heard and helped, maybe everyone can start talking to each other again. Let's be super kind!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree completely, Kenji. Kindness is the bridge that will bring us back together. Let us look for a solution that is not only fair in its rules, but warm in its spirit, so every neighbor feels truly valued.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Kindness is a sentiment, but stability is a result. If we prioritize warmth over a clear, sustainable distribution of labor, we will simply return to the same cycle of burnout and resentment. We must be precise about the workload.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're always so precise! But I'm with you! We need a plan where everyone actually does their part. No more ""cheating"" by letting one person do everything! Let's find the most fair and fun way!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such a spirited discussion. As we move forward, let us remember that true harmony is found when we protect the most vulnerable among us. A solution is only fair if it is affordable for all.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
