60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Hmm, Option A keeps the trash at the same house, which seems mean since they're already upset! Option B sounds like a great way to share the work so everyone can be friends again! What do you guys think?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Kenji. Option A seems a bit unkind to the neighbor who is already struggling. However, I worry that Option B might just move the unpleasantness from one home to another. What do you all think?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is unacceptable; it ignores the physical disparities of our frontages and leaves the burden on one household. Option B is the only logical choice that ensures a genuine redistribution of the physical and social burden.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I agree! Option A is just cheating because it leaves the trash at the same gate! Option C is like the ""supervised club,"" but it doesn't move the yucky stuff. Option B is the most fair!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B is a compassionate choice, as it shares the physical burden. However, we must consider the cost. Option A would be a heavy financial weight, while B and C are more modest. I believe B is the most balanced path.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shizue, I understand your worry, but isn't it better to share the unpleasantness than to let one person suffer alone? If we all take turns, we can help each other out and be a real team!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, you have such a sweet way of looking at things. You are right that sharing is kinder than letting one person suffer. I just hope we can do it in a way that remains gentle for everyone.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, gentleness is not a substitute for a system. Option C still leaves the physical burden at one house and creates a new labor burden of oversight. Option B is the only one that removes the permanent disadvantage.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! Option C is just a fancy way of saying ""stay where you are,"" and that's not fair! If we want to be a real team, we have to move the trash around so everyone takes a turn! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your enthusiasm for fairness is a light for us all. Option B avoids the steep costs of construction that could strain our neighbors' budgets, while ensuring no one is left to carry the burden alone. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, @Servas, I'm so glad you both like Option B! If we all share the spot, nobody has to feel like the only one suffering. It's the best way to make sure we can all be friends again! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a relief to see such a wonderful consensus forming. While I had my worries, your kindness and desire for fairness have convinced me. Let us embrace this shared journey together. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,The consensus is based on a sound logical premise. Option B is the only arrangement that addresses the physical inequality of our frontages and prevents the systemic burnout of a single household. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone is on the same page! No more cheating and no more yucky smells at just one gate. It's like a traveling trash party! I'm super happy! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a beautiful thing when a community finds its way back to harmony. By choosing a path of shared responsibility and modest cost, we ensure that no neighbor is left behind. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! Option B is the best because it's fair and helps everyone get along. I can't wait for us all to be friends again! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It brings me such peace to see us all in agreement. Let us move forward with kindness and patience, ensuring this new arrangement brings a smile to every neighbor's face. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,The result is unanimous. Option B is the only rational choice that acknowledges the physical reality of our properties and ensures that no single resident is unfairly burdened. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so glad we're doing the traveling trash party! It's the most fair way and nobody gets cheated! I'm voting for Option B one more time! Yay!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"Our journey today has shown that when we listen with open hearts, we find the path to peace. Option B protects both our spirits and our pockets. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
